  "id": "indeterminism",
  "term": "indeterminism",
  "definition": "Indeterminism is the view that mental change or development cannot always be completely explained by prior psychological states or outside conditions. In a stronger free-will sense, it treats willing as at least sometimes not fully determined by motives, or as itself deciding which motive becomes strongest.",
